d by your body to provide energy throughout all of these activities. You get that boost of energy to put up that extra rep, but also improve your endurance through boosted phosphocreatine stores, allowing you to sustain higher intensities for longer while working cardio. <br></p><br><p>Finally, creatine is associated with better water retention in muscles, improving cellular hydration. This improves both function and appearance - who doesn't love getting a pump in the gym after a workout?</p></span></div></div><picture data-rid="122fcaf5-f676-401a-a3d9-c3747624fb85" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0" class="r-h4dqt1"><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Infographic_CreatineBenefitsMap_WhiteBG_4_a5c5a9b8-b35f-46cb-b5b0-deaa2674153a.webp?v=1738701096&amp;width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Infographic_CreatineBenefitsMap_WhiteBG_4_a5c5a9b8-b35f-46cb-b5b0-deaa2674153a.webp?v=1738701096&amp;width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Infographic_CreatineBenefitsMap_WhiteBG_4_a5c5a9b8-b35f-46cb-b5b0-deaa2674153a.webp?v=1738701096&amp;width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Infographic_CreatineBenefitsMap_WhiteBG_4_a5c5a9b8-b35f-46cb-b5b0-deaa2674153a.webp?v=1738701096" alt="Circular diagram showing eight benefits of creatine, including increased energy and muscle growth." class="r-2sintm" loading="eager"/></picture></div><div data-rid="1fd8e3b9-0d68-4dc5-b2aa-f3053ae3baf9" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0" class="r-16o296h"><div data-rid="019ef076-90ac-459f-b3c9-43951f16cdaa" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0" class="r-d33fvd"><div data-rid="b7b710c5-e8cc-4ef8-9e42-b841c88b7306" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-1p67fcd"><div data-rid="cf943664-1a74-4e64-ac3e-4fa9c44cc655" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-u872s9"><div class="r-1i6gpeb"><video src="https://cdn.shopify.com/videos/c/o/v/cfc731d7cdae46ae97cecd7b701cce3a.mp4" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:var(--rof, inherit);object-position:var(--rop, inherit)" preload="metadata" autoplay="" muted="" loop=""></video></div></div></div><div data-rid="1cd4b9eb-ddcd-4bb9-99bd-35d4eb869633" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-rk6iw4"><div data-rid="564dbc0e-cb2a-4dcd-bcd6-bc8479c6e67c" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-1y35tql alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>2. Improves focus during long training sessions and competitions</p></span></div><div data-rid="ed453c9e-fa68-4b81-b046-35c865ea42c2" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-1u5wjda alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Creatine has been linked to improved brain function and reduced mental fatigue. This not only improves the efficacy of your workouts, but also allows you to stay focused and push through exhaustion during strenuous competitions like CrossFit, Hyrox, Spartan Races, and beyond.</p><p><br></p><p>Increased ATP production also isn't just present for muscular usage - additional ATP production also provides the brain with more energy, improving reaction time, concentration, and decision-making during races.</p><p><br></p><p>Beyond the clear muscular benefits, studies have shown that creatine has neuroprotective properties, which can reduce the stress and anxiety from increased cortisol levels present with intensive training.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="ced9280e-3d9b-4429-a84c-356116ac33eb" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0" data-alchemy-url-hashmark="influencers" tabindex="-1" id="influencers" data-alchemy-url-hashmark-ignore="true" class="r-16a5fur"><div data-rid="44a9c7ab-f4db-4ff4-98b8-a6652a70c6ec" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0" class="r-1s6uyv4"><div data-rid="1ea16d3f-444d-4a76-b812-6664253db09f" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-1codtpk alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>3. Improved recovery after workouts</p></span></div><div data-rid="a6a44385-cb08-4fe0-909a-785375c78047" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-1j0ahq8 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>All hybrid athletes have had at least that one workout where they feel like they can't get out of the bed the next day, let alone hit leg day. Intensive training regimens can result in muscle damage and inflammation over time.</p><p><br></p><p>Creatine has been shown to reduce muscle soreness and to speed up recovery, allowing you to train more frequently and just feel better the next day.</p></span></div></div><picture data-rid="f1919d91-9342-4663-9ef0-2137d225eb7a" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0" class="r-1hozwb"><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/DSC06171.jpg?v=1737502172&amp;width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/DSC06171.jpg?v=1737502172&amp;width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/DSC06171.jpg?v=1737502172&amp;width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/DSC06171.jpg?v=1737502172" alt="Man in gym examining a nutritional supplement container." class="r-73kiio" loading="eager"/></picture></div><div data-rid="2bfabcc7-196d-4916-94d4-abb83f4b2f3d" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0" data-alchemy-url-hashmark="benefits" tabindex="-1" id="benefits" data-alchemy-url-hashmark-ignore="true" class="r-8unsyx"><picture data-rid="a414c748-fa46-414f-9a15-5de048faa81c" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0" class="r-1bms9k3"><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/WadeHinmanOtherResize_aa92efa0-64ba-444a-abed-ad93bdb7be33.png?v=1739223466&amp;width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source 